cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use trace or its corpus, please cite it as below."
title: "trace: an agent-owned nixpkgs fork for merge-ready CVE evidence bundles"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Ad Astra Computing, Inc."
    website: "https://adastracomputing.com"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Ad-Astra-Computing/trace"
license: Apache-2.0
version: "0.7.0"
date-released: "2026-07-21"
abstract: >-
  trace turns known upstream security fixes into signed, auditable nixpkgs
  evidence bundles. A Patcher drafts a fix, a cross-family Reviewer critiques
  it cold, a Builder compiles the package twice (once without the fix, once
  with it) in a hermetic Nix sandbox, and a Steward signs the result only
  when the evidence supports it. Model output is never trusted by itself;
  schemas, hash-bound replay records, and signed canonical manifests carry
  the evidence.
